aps":61,"epa_per_play":-0.2251,"pass_rate":0.623,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5962,"def_epa_per_play":-0.0506},{"week":11,"opponent":"CHI","home":false,"pf":13.0,"pa":21.0,"off_snaps":70,"epa_per_play":-0.1263,"pass_rate":0.6857,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5455,"def_epa_per_play":-0.1039}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2023,"team":"LAC","distance":0.5661,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kellen Moore"},{"season":2024,"team":"LV","distance":0.6757,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"IND","distance":0.7072,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Frank Reich"},{"season":2024,"team":"CLE","distance":0.7699,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.7832,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Mike LaFleur"}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"CAR","distance":0.2048,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Ejiro Evero"},{"season":2025,"team":"DAL","distance":0.2792,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"WAS","distance":0.2911,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"DAL","distance":0.2935,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"LV","distance":0.3091,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Patrick Graham"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Saints are 3-7 through week 11 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 257 to 215. The offense ranks 22nd in EPA per play and the defense 19th in EPA allowed, so neither side has stood out much yet. Their most distinctive trait is the 3rd highest no-huddle rate in the league.","offense":"The Saints offense has been a little below average by EPA per play so far. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Schematically, they stand out for the 3rd highest no-huddle rate and a screen rate that was among the lowest in the league. Tyler Shough has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Chris Olave, who has drawn 28% of the targets.","defense":"The Saints defense has been a little below average by EPA allowed per play so far. Its strongest area has been sack rate, where it ranks 7th, and its weakest has been takeaways per game, where it ranks 27th. Chase Young has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is Colby Wooden, who has 3 sacks while playing only 48% of the snaps, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is a blitz rate that ranks 5th highest in the league.","special":"The Saints have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 70% of field goals, which is one of the worst in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into running backs, about 8% of the money on the books.","players":"Tyler Shough has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 2,395 yards. Chris Olave has been the clear top target with 28% of the looks and 866 receiving yards. The backfield has been a committee led by Kendre Miller and Travis Etienne. On defense, Carl Granderson leads the team with 8.5 sacks and Julian Blackmon has picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"Kellen Moore is calling the offense as head coach and Brandon Staley is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 Chargers under Kellen Moore and the 2024 Raiders. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Panthers under Ejiro Evero and the 2025 Cowboys.","trends":"The offense went from 27th in EPA per play in 2025 to 22nd so far this season, a modest improvement. The defense moved from 10th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 19th so far this season, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was fourth down go rate, which went from 54% to 31%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}